// Refined curved lattice x offset x MIRROR lower bound (review 7 Oct 2026,
// finding #9): a brush grafted at r = offset + 1 on a cylindrical domain
// whose inner boundary r = 3 is a MIRROR, at FJC_choices 5. The inward
// refined bonds that land in the fjc-deep lower ghost band are folded with
// a (site, image)-symmetric area, the inner twin of the outer-mirror fold;
// before the fix they used the unfolded area, which broke detailed balance:
// theta came out 59.94 instead of 60 and GN/mu/F depended on the chain
// orientation ((P)1(A)29 vs (A)29(P)1: mu -12.9995 vs -12.9589). The two
// starts below are the SAME molecule written in opposite directions, so the
// two kal rows must agree to the solver floor (and theta = 60 exactly).
// Also guards: kal lat n_layers reports the INPUT count (20), not the
// refined one (40) (#63); write_bounds keeps ZERO ghost rows on the
// integrand density columns, as Namics writes them (#76).
// No direct oracle: Namics shares the axis test (LGrad1.cpp) and places
// its refined shells at fjc x the offset (reported upstream), so the validation is
// the orientation identity + theta closure, plus the L-symmetry of the
// transfer operator (1e-16, checked when the fold landed).
lat : NN : n_layers : 20
lat : NN : geometry : cylindrical
lat : NN : lattice_type : simple_cubic
lat : NN : offset_first_layer : 3
lat : NN : FJC_choices : 5
lat : NN : lattice_type : hexagonal

mon : P : freedom : pinned
mon : P : pinned_range : 1;1
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_W : 0.4
mon : W : freedom : free

mol : pol : composition : (P)1(A)29
mol : pol : freedom : restricted
mol : pol : theta : 60

mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent

newton : NN : tolerance : 1e-10

output : kal : append : false
kal : mol : pol : theta
kal : mol : pol : GN
kal : mol : pol : mu
kal : mon : A : 1st_M_phi_z
kal : sys : NN : free_energy
kal : sys : NN : grand_potential
kal : lat : NN : n_layers

output : pro : append : false
output : pro : write_bounds : true
pro : mol : pol : phi
pro : sys : NN : grand_potential_density
start

mol : pol : composition : (A)29(P)1
start
